Initialize the linkedSignal with an object containing separate source and computation properties. This allows you to access previous state within the computation logic instead of resetting to a default value.

```ts
selectedOption = linkedSignal<ShippingMethod[], ShippingMethod>({
  source: this.shippingOptions,
  computation: (newOptions, previous) => {
    return newOptions.find((opt) => opt.id === previous?.value.id) ?? newOptions[0];
  },
});
```

The previous object provides access to both the old source value and the old linkedSignal value. You can use these properties to determine if the current selection remains valid within the new options list.

```ts
computation: (newOptions, previous) => {
  const oldSource = previous.source; // Previous value of the source signal
  const oldValue = previous.value;   // Previous value of this linkedSignal
  return ...;
}
```

