This pattern ensures proper tree-shaking by allowing the compiler to remove unused code from the client application bundle. Standard tokens might retain unused components in the bundle anyway due to how Angular stores them. Library developers must implement this to prevent retention of unused components when an application uses only some capabilities.

```typescript
