In zoneless applications, mutations like `FormArray.push()` don't automatically trigger change detection. You need to manually notify Angular:

```ts
import { Component, ChangeDetectorRef, inject } from '@angular/core';
import { takeUntilDestroyed } from '@angular/core/rxjs-interop';
import { FormArray } from '@angular/forms';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-profile-editor',
  templateUrl: './profile-editor.component.html'
})
export class ProfileEditor {
  private readonly cdr = inject(ChangeDetectorRef);

  constructor() {
    this.profileForm.valueChanges
      .pipe(takeUntilDestroyed())
      .subscribe(() => this.cdr.markForCheck());
  }

  get aliases(): FormArray {
    return this.profileForm.get('aliases') as FormArray;
  }

  addAlias() {
    this.aliases.push(this.fb.control(''));
    this.cdr.markForCheck();
  }
}
```

Key solutions:
1. Subscribe to `valueChanges` observable and call `markForCheck()` on change detection
2. Alternatively, manually invoke `cdr.markForCheck()` after form mutations
3. Use `takeUntilDestroyed()` to properly unsubscribe when component is destroyed

