After calling the `newActor()` method, you should imperatively clear all flags by invoking the form's `reset()` method. This restores the form to its initial state, hiding error messages and clearing validation flags.

Implementation in the component logic:
```ts
newActor() {
  // Logic to add new actor data
  this.form.reset();
}
```
This ensures clicking **New Actor** resets both the form values and its control flags.

To implement this pattern, wrap the form inputs in a container div bound to the `hidden` property of the `submitted` flag. When the form is submitted, set the flag to true to hide the inputs and display the result content using `*ngIf`. To allow re-editing, bind an Edit button's click event to a method that resets the flag.

```html
<div [hidden]="submitted">
  <!-- Form inputs -->
</div>

<div *ngIf="submitted">
  <!-- Read-only content -->
  <button (click)="resetForm()">Edit</button>
</div>
```

```typescript
submitted = false;

onSubmit() {
  this.submitted = true;
}

resetForm() {
  this.submitted = false;
}
```

