In the component class, use FormBuilder to create a FormGroup dynamically. Iterate over the model properties to add controls with specific validators.

```ts
// component.ts
import { Component, OnInit } from '@angular/core';
import { FormBuilder, FormGroup, Validators } from '@angular/forms';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-dynamic-form-question',
  templateUrl: './dynamic-form-question.component.html'
})
export class DynamicFormQuestionComponent implements OnInit {
  dynamicForm: FormGroup;

  constructor(private fb: FormBuilder) {}

  ngOnInit() {
    const { validators, properties } = this.questionModel;

    this.dynamicForm = this.fb.group({
      ...properties.reduce((acc, key) => ({
        ...acc,
        [key]: this.fb.control(null, validators[key])
      }), {})
    });
  }
}
```

The container component typically holds the root [formGroup] directive binding to the parent's FormGroup. The DynamicFormQuestionComponent creates child groups or controls within that structure using [formControlName]. Both rely on the ReactiveFormsModule for directives like [formGroup], [formControlName], and @switch.

