```html
@defer (on viewport; hydrate never) {
  <parent-content />
  <!-- Child hydration attempts are ignored -->
  <child-with-hydrate [hydrate]="true" />
} @placeholder {
  <div>Loading...</div>
}
```

Note that using `hydrate never` prevents hydration of the entire nested subtree. No other `hydrate` triggers fire for content nested underneath that block.

You combine both directives within the parentheses of the @defer statement, specifying `hydrate on` followed by the condition alongside the regular trigger. The following code demonstrates this pattern:

```html
